{"title":"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618a918d963a7a6c2934db2fd337c7c56ac8fea8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; r &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />.  Below are five equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  Which equation has the largest solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/87670fecb4a24fee91f26ccf345d7501b1aa43c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3(1 + r)^x = 7\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3(1 + r/10)^x = 7\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3(1 + 2r)^x = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"520\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cabe7a6d7e790c55efb7aa1663cfa7e5fe079f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3(1 + \\sqrt {r})^x = 7\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3(1 + 1/r)^x = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"344\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>(B)</b> Intuitively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> will be largest for that option for which the value in the parentheses is smallest.\n</p><p>Formally, first note that each of the values in parentheses is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which leads to the conclusion that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> will be the largest when the value of the parentheses is smallest. Now, each of the options is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0eb8eddef90a515326003d01a6671f0769d7646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3f(r)^x = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. This can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae8b0fc901a3def6150afa2e923eafa54276fc8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\log f(r) = \\log\\frac 73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d109a3f715d746523840b4603534398e37a78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r)&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/45739a2b1d04ed93b5eba47aadb6f36484beb1e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log f(r)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the largest for the option for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed66420129e21c0c0e72c21558750e7c04b3b89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log f(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> is smallest. And as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed66420129e21c0c0e72c21558750e7c04b3b89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log f(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> is an increasing function, this is the option for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d404a4bf3e67e6fd88a82c768979219e455e3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is smallest.\n</p><p>We now get the following easier problem: Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f8fd8b742a09b42eb620851526ff44732a448c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;r&lt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, find the smallest value in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/1864771825af631fcfa9126e3e195c2620ef26dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 1+r, 1+r/10, 1+2r, 1+\\sqrt r, 1+1/r\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/116e6ecec919528befe7e814a12b484bdcb97435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+r/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> is smaller than the first and the third option. \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192e72acd73a37b62dda4ba63b320cbabb8ab45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49de2adfaf910759ea05607eb07c363009ec392c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10r$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712735ad2549e79652b1eb859575d7484a73f54b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r/10 &lt; 1/r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>And finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289e784712c93240a3e76184dcd45efbdc84583e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r/100 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240f7a3036653d855f07f39c205718f18b6fe5fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2/100 &lt; r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" />, and as both sides are positive, we can take the square root and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf13860b38908c9930b2d9e04390f076bbfa68c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r/10 &lt; \\sqrt r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/429a820f96d5a9de225c7c3202add78938ab5469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 3\\left(1+\\frac{r}{10}\\right)^x = 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As stated in the first solution, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> will be largest when the value in the parenthesis is smallest.\n</p><p>We can plug in a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (for instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a0736cc24657e4fbe87410091de1c4ebd44e26db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />) and see which parenthesis has the smallest value. Doing so, we see that B is the answer.\n</p><p>-Made_in_2004\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B\">2009 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221243\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 242/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5399/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.894      1 -total\n 58.36%    7.525      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.24%    5.060      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7929:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221243 and revision id 259754. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}